#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked of the `verdict` output of 'Check the pins' in .github/workflows/upstream-pins.yml, which runs `check:upstream-pins --out`. Exit 0 is every pin current, 1 at least one behind, 2 could not tell; an exit 1 with no report file is a crash and is reclassified as could-not-tell, as is any other code. `no` is verdict == 'unknown': 'Refuse to report success on an undetermined pin' runs `exit 1` and the tracking issue is left untouched. `yes` is verdict != 'unknown', the guard on ensuring the `upstream-pin` label."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked of the same `verdict`. `no` is verdict == 'current': the tracking issue is closed because every pin is current. `yes` is verdict == 'behind': the one tracking issue is opened or edited in place."
msgstr ""

