msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — left alone"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One issue, edited in place. GitHub's own failure mail is the channel that was already ignored thirty times, so this adds none: an edit does not notify, and a pin that stays behind for two months stays one unread item rather than nine."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open or EDIT the one tracking issue"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:90
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns exactly three outcomes and must keep them visibly different: current closes the tracking issue, behind opens or edits it, and UNKNOWN leaves the issue untouched while failing the job anyway — a watchdog that goes blind must never read as clean, so this lane is the one place that distinction cannot be collapsed into a single pass or fail. It hands off at the first sign of judgement: the moment a bump needs adopting, that is Lane_Agent's, never this one's."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:79
#. Diagram label
msgid "Pick up the stale pin"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:55
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the pin registry upstream-pins.json"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:95
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:80
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The hand-off from the mechanical lane to the one that can exercise judgement. Claiming the bean here is what stops two sessions adopting the same bump."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:56
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The registry lists the tenants and says, per row, WHICH FILE holds the pin literal and how to read it. It deliberately does not store the version: one answer to \"what are we running\", read from the file the build reads."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reusable subprocess. Every pinned dependency enters it the same way, so a new tenant is a registry row and a call — never a second diagram saying the same thing in different words."
msgstr ""

